'' A bydesc parameter takes an array of exactly its element type (fbc error 58): a
'' different UDT is refused and so is a DERIVED one -- there is no slicing through a
'' descriptor. A static member variable belongs to a toplevel type (fbc error 264): a
'' type declared inside a SCOPE block or a SUB is refused, one inside a namespace is not.
'' Matches fbc on lines 36 and 37; the two nested statics report on the 'static' line
'' (42, 49) where fbc reports on the 'end type' that follows (43, 50).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/bydesc-and-nested-static.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' GOLDEN: expected/bydesc-and-nested-static.out
